  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Answer with bounded evidence",
      "items": [
        "Retrieval filters institution, effective dates, jurisdiction, confidentiality and product. Parent sections must match scope; otherwise child evidence is retained.",
        "Linked circulars are assembled completely. Context packing uses a token budget; missing required amendments cause abstention.",
        "The chain validates citation IDs and exact evidence quotes, with at most two drafts. These checks do not prove semantic correctness."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Quality and human feedback",
      "items": [
        "Live evaluation reuses one retrieval and scores the final answer/context: faithfulness, answer relevancy, context precision and context recall. Precision/recall need a reference.",
        "The chat shows an answer, citations and a Datadog link. RAGAS scores belong in Datadog; unavailable metrics are not invented.",
        "Feedback is stored first. Submitter + submission IDs make retries idempotent. Datadog thumbs require enabled LLM Observability and a target span; SDK failure does not undo persistence.",
        "Feedback listing and review require a configured bearer token. This is local training authentication, not enterprise SSO."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Ingestion and repeatable evaluation",
      "items": [
        "Ingestion reads authoritative register entries and PDFs, chunks clauses/tables, and embeds changed children before updating parent sections. There is no cross-collection transaction or job lock.",
        "Batch evaluation imports shared RAG and scorer code; it does not call the FastAPI server. It resolves references, runs golden cases and writes a local JSON report.",
        "RAG and quality nodes are shared library responsibilities within API/CLI processes, not additional deployed services."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Telemetry is a configured flow",
      "items": [
        "Mac applications send APM/LLM data to loopback port 18126 and DogStatsD to 18125. Docker maps these to Agent ports 8126 and 8125. The Agent forwards to Datadog.",
        "When enabled, instrumentation records requests, database/model calls, token usage and versioned prompt annotations. Batch evaluation also submits scores when enabled.",
        "JSON logs go to stdout and need separate log collection. /health is liveness; /metrics and /metrics/latency are process-local. Queued telemetry is not proof of cloud receipt."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Reading this architecture",
      "items": [
        "Choose Live for motion, Still for static viewing, and a guided view to focus a workflow. Select any component for its source passport.",
        "This is a source-backed illustration of the latest working code, not a live traffic monitor. Exact source bytes are committed only in an isolated local snapshot; nothing was published. See SOURCE_NOTES.md for the working-tree provenance.",
        "Dense retrieval is the default; hybrid search needs a manual text index and reranking is optional. LangGraph and application MCP are future layers. No LangSmith integration is depicted."
      ]
    }
  ]
